    "scope": "exact no-go for termwise conductor-uniform externalization of the universal phase/incidence kernel; the actual native image would inherit the rank of its occupied residue cells, which has not been classified. This is not a no-go for a source-specific sparse image or an assembled signed relative complex that cancels the constituent before Adams extraction.",
    "statement": "The universal Artin-Schreier phase block has rank Q-1 on all residues and rank m on every proper m-cell restriction; its Wick-centered incidence image has the same ranks. Thus a source-independent adapter valid on a full physical sector has rank comparable with Q=q^a, exponential in the place degree a. The natural AS line and diagonal incidence class also fail independent partial Frobenius invariance."
